From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: lemans-evk: map PCIe1 switch RIDs in base DT

The default FIT configuration for the IQ-9075 EVK loads lemans-evk.dtb
without the staging overlay.  The PCIe1 QPS615 switch therefore needs its
complete requester-ID to SMMU SID map in the base board DT.

The live board has switch ports at RIDs 0x208 through 0x238 and Intel
Ethernet endpoints at 0x400 and 0x500.  Use the established sequential
switch mapping with PCIe1's SID base at 0x80.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
@@ -850,6 +850,17 @@
 &pcie1 {
 	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	iommu-map = <0x0   &pcie_smmu 0x80 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x100 &pcie_smmu 0x81 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x208 &pcie_smmu 0x82 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x210 &pcie_smmu 0x83 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x218 &pcie_smmu 0x84 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x220 &pcie_smmu 0x85 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x228 &pcie_smmu 0x86 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x230 &pcie_smmu 0x87 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x238 &pcie_smmu 0x88 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x400 &pcie_smmu 0x89 0x0 0x1>,
+		    <0x500 &pcie_smmu 0x8a 0x0 0x1>;
 
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie1_default_state>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-- 
